"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[7590],{49985:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"new","desc":"Builds the service. A [Matchmaker] constructs one as `queue.quickplay` on\\nfirst access and writes nothing until a method is called.","params":[{"name":"store","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"settings","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"deps","desc":"","lua_type":"any?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"any\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":169,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"host","desc":"Advertises this server as joinable.\\n\\nCall it once the match server is ready to take players, with whatever a\\njoining server needs to reach you:\\n\\n```lua\\nqueue.quickplay:host({ data = { accessCode = code, placeId = ARENA_PLACE } })\\n```\\n\\n`data` is delivered verbatim as `assignment.data` and must survive a JSON\\nround trip, within `quickPlay.maxListingDataBytes` (1024).\\n\\n`capacity` defaults to `quickPlay.capacity`, which defaults to `size.max`.\\nThe player count is read from `playerCount` on every heartbeat, defaulting to\\nthe `Players` service.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"options","desc":"","lua_type":"HostOptions"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Result<HostedListing>"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":256,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"_beat","desc":"One heartbeat for one hosted listing: refresh the count, retire fulfilled\\nreservations, migrate to a new lane if the layout moved, and rewrite the\\nindex entry.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"handle","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"force","desc":"","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":352,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"_searchOrder","desc":"The lanes to walk this pass, starting somewhere random.\\n\\nSpreading searchers over lanes rather than starting everyone at lane 0 is\\nwhat keeps a resize from turning into a stampede on one map. With one lane,\\nwhich is where a small game sits, this is a single read.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"count","desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"{ number }\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":428,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"search","desc":"Looks for a seat and takes it.\\n\\nReturns `ok(nil)` when nothing joinable was found, which is the ordinary\\n\\"everything is full\\" outcome and not an error: the caller stays queued.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"request","desc":"`partition`, `size`, `userIds`.","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Result<{ listingId: string, reservationId: string, listing: Listing }?>"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":448,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"_claimAny","desc":"Tries the head of the viable candidates until one of them yields a seat.\\n\\nThe head is sampled rather than taken in order. The index is sorted fullest\\nfirst, which is the right *policy* but the wrong thing for every lobby in the\\nfleet to act on at the same instant, so each searcher starts somewhere\\nslightly different within the few fullest matches.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"viable","desc":"","lua_type":"{ ListingView }"},{"name":"partition","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"size","desc":"","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"userIds","desc":"","lua_type":"{ number }"},{"name":"now","desc":"","lua_type":"number\\n"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"any?\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":498,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"release","desc":"Hands a claimed seat back. Call it when the teleport you were holding it for\\ndid not happen.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"listingId","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"reservationId","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"False when the reservation was already gone.","lua_type":"Result<boolean>"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":541,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"listings","desc":"The joinable listings in a partition, fullest first, for a server browser or\\na debug command.\\n\\nReads every lane, so prefer [QuickPlay:search] for anything on a hot path.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"partition","desc":"","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Result<{ ListingView }>"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":566,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"get","desc":"Reads one listing record by id.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"listingId","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Result<Listing?>"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":591,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"step","desc":"Heartbeats whichever hosted listings are due. Driven by the queue\'s worker\\npass, so `queue:step()` covers it.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"mono","desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":608,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"hostedCount","desc":"Hosted listings on this server, for [Matchmaker:health].","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"number\\n"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":632,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}},{"name":"closeAll","desc":"Delists everything this server is hosting.\\n\\nCalled from [Matchmaker:stop], so a match server bound to `game:BindToClose`\\nstops taking players the moment it starts shutting down rather than after\\n`listingExpiration`. A server that dies without this is cleaned up by expiry\\nanyway; this only makes it immediate.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":650,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"QuickPlay","desc":"Backfilling players into matches that are already running.\\n\\nMuster\'s ordinary path only ever forms *new* matches. Quick Play adds the\\nother one: a live match server advertises itself, and a queued player who\\nfits drops straight into it instead of waiting for a fresh lobby to fill.\\n\\nIt is off unless a queue asks for it, since it is a casual-mode feature:\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal casual = Muster.new({ name = \\"casual\\", size = 8, quickPlay = true })\\n```\\n\\nQuick Play **ignores rating entirely**. There is no window, no relaxation and\\nno banding; a listing with a free seat takes the next player who wants it. Do\\nnot turn it on for a ranked queue.\\n\\n### On the match server\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal listing = Muster.Result.unwrap(casual.quickplay:host({\\n\\tdata = { accessCode = code, placeId = ARENA_PLACE },\\n}))\\n\\nlisting:setOpen(false)  -- round underway; stop taking players\\nlisting:close()         -- delist immediately\\n```\\n\\nThe handle is kept up to date by the queue\'s own worker pass, so a match\\nserver needs one `Muster.new` and one `host` call. Its player count refreshes\\nevery `heartbeatInterval` (30 s), and a server that dies is delisted by\\n`listingExpiration` (90 s) without anybody cleaning up.\\n\\n### In the lobby\\n\\n```lua\\ncasual.quickPlayMatched:connect(function(assignment)\\n\\tTeleportService:TeleportToPrivateServer(\\n\\t\\tassignment.data.placeId, assignment.data.accessCode, players)\\nend)\\n\\ncasual:quickPlay(player.UserId)\\n```\\n\\n[Matchmaker:quickPlay] writes an ordinary ticket flagged for backfill and then\\nlooks for a seat immediately. **If every listed match is full the player just\\nstays in the normal queue** and forms a fresh match the usual way, retrying\\nthe search every `searchInterval` while they wait. There is no separate queue\\nand no dead end: the two paths race, and whichever resolves first wins.\\n\\n### Taking the last seat\\n\\nEvery claim is a compare-and-set on the listing record, so when fifty lobby\\nservers see the same 7/8 match, exactly one of them gets the seat and the rest\\nmove on to their next candidate. Claimed seats are held as reservations until\\nthe players arrive, which is what stops two lobbies from both filling a slot\\ninside one heartbeat window. See [Listings].\\n\\n### Lanes\\n\\nA MemoryStore range read returns at most 200 items, so listings shard into\\nlanes exactly as tickets do, by hash, with the layout stamped into every key.\\nThe count starts at one and doubles once a lane is consistently too full to\\nread in one go, so a game with six live matches pays for none of it. Pin it\\nwith `quickPlay.lanes` if you would rather.","source":{"line":71,"path":"src/QuickPlay.luau"}}')}}]);